      "repair_reason": "- No automated repair is needed; this PR is already the narrow implementation candidate and only normal maintainer merge gating remains.; Cleared: The diff only changes a local Feishu timer binding and does not touch secrets, dependencies, workflows, package resolution, downloads, permissions, or other security-sensitive surfaces. (sha=521be79e84ea93242109afc79bab4c18edb0d0de)",
      "review_summary": "The PR hoists the Feishu `waitForAbortableDelay` timer handle into an earlier `let` binding so cleanup can read an initialized value before the timeout is assigned.\n\nPR surface: Source +1. Total +1 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: no. there is not a high-confidence live current-main reproduction. Source inspection shows `finish()` would read a later `const timer` if the pre-timer cleanup branch runs, but I did not establish a failing native runtime path.",
